      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "First thought, if it really is tied to the language and not the locale, that is a straight-up bug, because most English-speaking regions will want \"dd/MM/yyyy\" and not \"MM/dd/yyyy\".\n\nSecond thought, yeah, Australia has a history of getting really cursed date formats via ICU, and being able to customise them to something acceptable while waiting for ICU to fix their shit is sort of essential. We were, for a while, cursed with a format like \"30 Apr. 2024\". Yeah, including the period after \"Apr\". When they did that update and we shipped it, we got half a dozen complaints in the first day.\n\nThird thought, https://xkcd.com/1179/",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
