      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As someone who sets the OS to always use ISO 8601 yyyy-MM-dd, having date/time format tied to locale seems absurd. No matter the language I want to see VRC UI in, my date format preference doesn't change. Why can't the date format be fetched from the OS? \n\nMost other software seems to have no issues with that (except Discord, but it at least has UK English with marginally more sane date format). \n\nAs a random thought, why on earth does toki pona use the US-centric MM/dd/yyyy? Which part of the language spec, that barely has any numbers to begin with, dictates that date format?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
